# UI Parity — Nest Migration (Hard Rule)

When moving features from legacy Next (`app/`) to Nest + `apps/web`:

## NEVER
- Simplify, restyle, or invent a “cleaner” UI
- Replace a full page with a stub (title + one paragraph)
- Remove sections, filters, cards, hero interactions, or empty-state UX
- Change layout structure (sidebar filters → top bar, etc.) without explicit product approval

## ALWAYS
- Port the **existing** legacy JSX/layout first
- Wire **data only** to Nest (`catalog`, `booking`, …)
- Keep palette/brand tokens as already used in the source page (do not “improve”)
- If a Nest endpoint is missing: keep UI + loading/empty states; do not delete the UI

## Source of truth
Legacy screens under `app/(dashboard)/*`, `app/(auth)/*`, `app/components/*`.

## Checklist before finishing a migration task
- [ ] Side-by-side: legacy page vs `apps/web` — same sections and hierarchy
- [ ] No developer-only empty copy (“Legacy site pnpm dev…”)
- [ ] Filters / cards / CTAs present if they existed in legacy
